  "stem": "The sum of the first \\(n\\) positive integers is \\(\\frac{n(n + 1)}{2}\\). If the sum of the first \\(n\\) positive integers is 210, what is the value of \\(n\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "20"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Set \\(\\frac{n(n + 1)}{2} = 210\\), so \\(n^{2} + n = 420\\).",
    "Then \\(n^{2} + n - 420 = 0\\), which factors as \\((n + 21)(n - 20) = 0\\).",
    "Since \\(n\\) is positive, \\(n = 20\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "n = symbols('n', positive=True)\nsol = solve(Eq(n*(n + 1)/2, 210), n)\nassert sol == [20]\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == sol",
